<title>PORTUGAL: POLL-Portugal 10-yr bond sale seen 6.37/6.42 pct.</title>
<headline>POLL-Portugal 10-yr bond sale seen 6.37/6.42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a forecast by five banks and a broker of the result of tomorrow's auction of 25 billion escudos of 10-year Portuguese bonds, without counting a tranche of 33 percent set aside for market makers.</p>
<p>Results of the auction are due around 1000 GMT. ----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>- BIDS:Min/Avg/Max	 (3 June 1997)</p>
<p>    MIN     6.35%/6.370%/6.40%   vs  last auction:6.50%</p>
<p>    AVG:     6.37%/6.402%/6.42%  vs  last auction:6.5594%</p>
<p>    MAX:     6.40%/6.423%/6.45%   vs last auction:6.58%</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>- PLACING :</p>
<p>    YES: 2		  vs   last auction: 19.910 bln esc</p>
<p>NO: 4</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Cls (30 June) OTC: 6.37 pct</p>
<p>Spread close Feb 2007 Portuguese bonds vs Feb 2007 Spanish Bonos</p>
<p>(6.36 pct): 1 bp</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Most bids at the auction should come in at rates higher than today's secondary market close, dealers said, especially because of the uncertain outcome of tomorrow's FOMC meeting.</p>
<p>Dealers said they did not expect all the bonds to be placed and noted that they did not expect them to be placed at more than five basis points above equivalent Bonos.</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>----Srgio Gonalves, Lisboa Editorial, 351-1-3150035</p>
